  It is a tall order, to say the least. Nothing I say can change the fact that there exists a vast gulf of power between them.

  But the lady does not dismiss me out of hand. She gazes at the flowers, thinking.

  Is she remembering what she saw in the courtyard that day? For an instant, I seem to glimpse a boy's flushed cheeks reflected in her eyes.

